---
import BasicLayout from '../layouts/BasicLayout.astro';
---

<BasicLayout title="How this site is built" intro="A short note on the tools, choices and checks behind robertwood.me.">
  <h2>Stack</h2>
  <p>
    Built with Astro and TypeScript. Pages are static HTML and CSS, with JavaScript only for the theme switch. Content
    lives in typed collections, so case studies and tools share one template each.
  </p>
  <h2>Design</h2>
  <p>
    The colours are muted CMYK inks on warm paper: a nod to my years in print design. Light and dark themes come from one
    set of CSS custom properties, and the site follows your device's setting unless you choose otherwise.
  </p>
  <h2>Accessibility</h2>
  <p>
    Every page is tested automatically against WCAG 2.2 AA in both themes before it's published, including colour
    contrast, keyboard focus and target sizes. If you find a barrier, please <a href="mailto:hello@robertwood.me">let me
    know</a>.
  </p>
</BasicLayout>
